        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Most wooden walking pads are ordinary motorised pads with a wood-look
          finish, and they should be bought on belt length, motor rating, capacity and warranty like any
          other.</strong> The finish is a matter of taste and should not cost extra. Genuinely wooden machines —
          Walkolution's manual desk treadmills from $2,995 and NOHrD's treadmills from about $8,199 — are a
          different, far more expensive category built for quiet daily walking or premium running.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy a solid-wood manual treadmill only if you will walk at a desk most days and value near-silence and
          longevity enough to pay for them. Otherwise, start with our
